{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And you shall make et the altar.</b> It says <b>the altar</b> and does not say 'an altar.' Perhaps this is because it refers back to what was mentioned in the general commandment, as it is written (Exodus 25:9): ״אֶת תַּבְנִית הַמִּשְׁכָּן וְאֶת תַּבְנִית כָּל כֵּלָיו״, and there He showed him the altar. Therefore it says <b>and you shall make et the altar</b> — the form of which I showed you; it must be hollow inside, of acacia wood."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:46.693820294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}